133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 91 0 R
/T (Many organizations are becoming more selective with hiring while continuing to seek access to top talent. They remain cautious about adding headcount, but also still prioritize candidates who can generate revenue, bring specialized expertise, or provide a clear strategic advantage. Organizations are now starting to leverage AI to automate high-volume, entry level recruiting needs. This allows talent acquisition teams to spend more time on strategic hiring needs, building candidate relationships, and reaffirming partnerships with recruiting firms that can identify high-potential talent.)
/E (Many organizations are becoming more selective with hiring while continuing to seek access to top talent. They remain cautious about adding headcount, but also still prioritize candidates who can generate revenue, bring specialized expertise, or provide a clear strategic advantage. Organizations are now starting to leverage AI to automate high-volume, entry level recruiting needs. This allows talent acquisition teams to spend more time on strategic hiring needs, building candidate relationships, and reaffirming partnerships with recruiting firms that can identify high-potential talent.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 91 0 R
/T (Candidates aren't more selective now because the market has drastically changed; they're more selective because they can now verify information in five minutes that once required a warm introduction to uncover. Ten years ago, a partner at a law firm evaluating a lateral move only used to have the firm's pitch, a Chambers ranking, and their personal network used to know. Information was scarce, so the firm did most of the persuading. Now there is more information at our fingertips than ever before. )
/E (Candidates aren't more selective now because the market has drastically changed; they're more selective because they can now verify information in five minutes that once required a warm introduction to uncover. Ten years ago, a partner at a law firm evaluating a lateral move only used to have the firm's pitch, a Chambers ranking, and their personal network used to know. Information was scarce, so the firm did most of the persuading. Now there is more information at our fingertips than ever before. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
