/Title (The biggest challenge for talent acquisition moving forward is uncertainty, which can slow decision making even when there is an urgent need for hiring. Organizations balancing new advancements with caution, while continuing to evaluate how changing market conditions and evolving technologies will affect workforce planning and actual headcount needs.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 294 0 R
/Prev 525 0 R
/Next 461 0 R
>>
endobj
527 0 obj
<<
/Title (Many organizations are becoming more selective with hiring while continuing to seek access to top talent. They remain cautious about adding headcount, but also still prioritize candidates who can generate revenue, bring specialized expertise, or provide a clear strategic advantage. Organizations are now starting to leverage AI to automate high-volume, entry level recruiting needs. This allows talent acquisition teams to spend more time on strategic hiring needs, building candidate relationships, and reaffirming partnerships with recruiting firms that can identify high-potential talent.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 461 0 R
/Next 589 0 R
>>
endobj
