/Title (Candidates aren't more selective now because the market has drastically changed; they're more selective because they can now verify information in five minutes that once required a warm introduction to uncover. Ten years ago, a partner at a law firm evaluating a lateral move only used to have the firm's pitch, a Chambers ranking, and their personal network used to know. Information was scarce, so the firm did most of the persuading. Now there is more information at our fingertips than ever before.)
