690 0 obj
<<
/Title (right hire. Organizations should focus on the metrics that reflect quality, speed, and long-term outcomes. The goal is not simply to track activity, but to understand what is driving success)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 656 0 R
/Prev 673 0 R
/Next 691 0 R
>>
endobj
691 0 obj
<<
/Title (and where the process may be creating unnecessary obstacles.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 656 0 R
/Prev 690 0 R
/Next 674 0 R
>>
endobj
692 0 obj
<<
/Title (These changes are already influencing how organizations are approaching the talent landscape. To better understand how these changes are playing out, we spoke with Larry Brand, a seasoned talent acquisition leader and Operating Partner at One Rock Capital Partners. Brand shares his perspectives on the future)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 592 0 R
/Prev 676 0 R
/Next 677 0 R
>>
endobj
693 0 obj
<<
/Title (The State of Talent Acquisition in Professional Services)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 677 0 R
>>
endobj
694 0 obj
<<
/Title (Companies should start thinking more strategically about future talent needs rather than waiting to recruit when the role becomes open. The best teams regularly evaluate where they are vulnerable, where succession planning is needed, and where technology may change the type of talent required. Waiting until there is an urgent vacancy puts organizations at a disadvantage.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 682 0 R
/Next 702 0 R
>>
endobj
695 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 682 0 R
/Prev 703 0 R
>>
endobj
696 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 683 0 R
/Next 704 0 R
>>
endobj
697 0 obj
<<
/Title (For example, we recently placed a candidate with a client we have worked with for more than 15 years. The hiring manager was intentional about looking beyond the immediate role, identifying someone who could be promoted within 12 to 18 months. Just as importantly, the candidate was expected to bring expertise that could elevate the existing team by training and developing employees in their current roles. That ability to strengthen the broader team was a key consideration in the hiring decision.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 683 0 R
/Prev 704 0 R
>>
endobj
698 0 obj
<<
/Title (The highest performing talent acquisition teams do more than just fill the position. They influence workforce strategy by understanding the actual business challenge the organization is trying to solve and aligning the right talent to address it. Every successful search should begin with the business challenge, and not with finding someone who matches the job description. This alignment between talent and business needs leads to better stronger partnerships with leadership, stronger talent, and greater long-term impact for the organization.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 684 0 R
/Next 699 0 R
>>
endobj
699 0 obj
<<
/Title (Specialization creates better outcomes. Deep industry knowledge and functional expertise will hold the most capital. High-performing talent acquisition teams build their teams around experts in the specific industries and functions they serve. This allows them to better understand the market, identify relevant talent, and assess candidates against the specific challenges and requirements of an organization.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 684 0 R
/Prev 698 0 R
>>
endobj
700 0 obj
<<
/Title (The second offer was from a mid-sized regional firm with a lower base salary, a 1,850- hour requirement with pro-bono work counting toward it, and a credit for work she originated.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 629 0 R
/Prev 687 0 R
/Next 705 0 R
>>
endobj
701 0 obj
<<
/Title (At the larger firm, during the interview process, three different people described the practice group differently, and no one could tell her to whom she would report.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 629 0 R
/Prev 705 0 R
/Next 688 0 R
>>
endobj
